cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite it as below."
title: "Once-reinforced random walk on Z^d has range exponent at least d/(d+1)"
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/nitromannitol/ORRW-Lower-Bound"
abstract: >-
  A machine-checked Lean 4 and Mathlib formalization of the paper
  "Once-reinforced random walk on Z^d has range exponent at least d/(d+1)"
  (Bou-Rabee and Peres): for d >= 2 and reinforcement beta >= 1 the expected
  range of once-reinforced random walk satisfies
  E|R_n| >= c beta^(-d/(d+1)) n^(d/(d+1)) (Theorem 1.1), with a
  stretched-exponential lower tail (Theorem 1.2) and the almost-sure bound it
  implies, a bound on the occupation measure (Theorem 1.3), and every lemma
  and proposition behind them.  Nothing is assumed: the development contains
  no sorry, no custom axiom and no cited result taken as a hypothesis, and each
  of the four main results has a Mathlib-only comparator challenge.
authors:
  - family-names: Bou-Rabee
    given-names: Ahmed
keywords:
  - Lean
  - mathlib
  - formal verification
  - once-reinforced random walk
  - self-interacting random walk
  - probability
license: Apache-2.0
references:
